QuranTester Cursor Rules (concise)

General
- Keep UI Arabic; write commit messages in English.
- Never commit secrets. Use .env (SMTP_*, DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET). Ensure .env is gitignored.
- Prefer minimal edits over refactors; reuse existing components and styles.
- Use absolute paths in tool calls and file references.

Tech Guardrails
- Frontend stack: React 19 + Vite with built-in hooks; no new state managers or UI kits without approval.
- Data fetching goes through `src/api.js` using native fetch; do not add axios/GraphQL clients.
- Styling lives in `index.css` (Cairo font, CSS variables, utility classes); avoid Tailwind, styled-components, or new preprocessors.
- Tables use `@tanstack/react-table`; reuse existing helpers instead of adding grid libraries.
- PDF/Excel exports are handcrafted (DOM/Blob); don’t introduce jsPDF/xlsx libraries unless requested.
- Icons rely on Font Awesome classes already wired; no alternative icon packs.
- Backend: Express + `pg` + raw SQL migrations (`server/src/db`); skip ORMs/framework swaps.
- File uploads already managed with multer(memory)+sharp; keep this pipeline.

Frontend (quran-tester-app)
- Dev: cd /Volumes/ExtremeSSD/Projects/QuranTester/quran-tester-app && npm install && npm run dev (5173)
- API base: VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
- Exports: use public/quran.png in PDF/Excel headers.
- Display: show Thumun as "id - name" and include Naqza in UI and exports.
- Free mode controls: single vertical column, centered; unify card/control width (~720px).
- Mobile: prevent horizontal overflow; cards full width.

Backend (server)
- Dev: cd /Volumes/ExtremeSSD/Projects/QuranTester/server && npm install && npm run dev (PORT=4000)
- DB: docker compose up -d, then npm run migrate; npm run seed (optional).
- Auth: login by username or email; email-based password reset via /auth/forgot and /auth/reset.
- Uploads: POST /students/:id/photo → multer(memory)+sharp to 128/256/512 JPEG; served under /uploads.
- Sessions: on pass, increment current_naqza; date-range overview at GET /sessions/overview?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD.
- Removed field: Do NOT add "notes" back anywhere (UI/API/DB).

Database & Migrations
- Path: /Volumes/ExtremeSSD/Projects/QuranTester/server/src/db/migrations
- Apply with: cd server && npm run migrate

Scoring Policy (for UI labels)
- Pass/fail based ONLY on Fatha: <4 pass, ≥4 fail. Grade is descriptive.

Security & Ops
- If port 4000 is busy: lsof -ti:4000 | xargs kill -9
- Serve uploads with long cache headers; do not expose filesystem paths.
- Don’t log sensitive env values.

Git Workflow
- Branch: main. Small, focused commits.
- If README was edited on GitHub: git pull --rebase origin main before push.
- Push: git push origin main

Cursor Execution Preferences
- Prefer semantic code search over broad grep; avoid noisy terminal greps.
- Use edit tools to change files; avoid ad-hoc terminal-based file mutations.
- Keep changes minimal, readable, and lint-clean. Avoid adding new deps unless required.

